    "result_text": "Green. Done.\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule by mirroring the existing telephone-uniqueness feature, adding small cohesive units rather than growing any existing method:\n\n- **`RequireUniqueEmail`** (new function, one method) \u2014 scans owners and throws when the request's lower-cased email matches an existing owner's (case-insensitive). Email is optional, so a null email is skipped.\n- **`DuplicateEmailException`** + **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler`** \u2014 the checked escalation and its 409 handler.\n- **`...DuplicateEmailException.yml`** \u2014 wires the handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserts a `uniqueEmail` step right after `NormaliseEmail` (which already lower-cases the request email), before `unique`.\n\nEach new class has zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other = 0), and the only existing file edited was the POST pipeline YAML (a small insertion), keeping structural impact low. The new acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass.",
